 was instrumental in pushing the boundaries of rock 'n' roll, notably influencing the development of hard rock and psychedelic rock genres. Known for their high-energy performances, they popularized the \"rave-up\" style, where a song builds in tempo and intensity, a technique that later found its way into heavy metal.\r\n\r\nIn 1992, they were inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame as performers, with the band continuing to tour under the leadership of Jim McCarty with a constantly evolving lineup.\r\n\r\nThe band created by [a=Todd Rundgren] aka [a=NAZZ] named their group after the Yardbirds' song \"The Nazz Are Blue\" ","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:262455","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":12886820,"name":"Metropolis Blues Quintet"}],"groups":null,"members":[{"active":false,"id":17827,"name":"Eric Clapton"},{"active":false,"id":25884,"name":"Mark Feltham"},{"active":false,"id":49624,"name":"Jeff Beck"},{"active":false,"id":180585,"name":"Jimmy Page"},{"active":true,"id":208175,"name":"Alan Glen"},{"active":true,"id":240349,"name":"Kenny Aaronson"},{"active":true,"id":256148,"name":"Earl Slick"},{"active":false,"id":274221,"name":"Paul Samwell-Smith"},{"active":false,"id":295369,"name":"Jerry Donahue"},{"active":false,"id":445544,"name":"Keith Relf"},{"active":true,"id":524748,"name":"Jim McCarty"},{"active":false,"id":558713,"name":"Rod Demick"},{"active":false,"id":594542,"name":"Chris Dreja"},{"active":false,"id":882220,"name":"Ray Majors"},{"active":false,"id":967024,"name":"John Idan"},{"active":false,"id":1199946,"name":"John Knightsbridge"},{"active":true,"id":1363613,"name":"Myke Scavone"},{"active":false,"id":1459091,"name":"Top Topham"},{"active":false,"id":3044682,"name":"Ben King (8)"},{"active":true,"id":3044683,"name":"Andy Mitchell (5)"},{"active":false,"id":10763125,"name":"John Philip Mayo"}],"namevariations":["Les Yardbirds","Los Yardbirds","The Yard Birds","The Yard-Birds","TheYardbirds","Yarbirds","Yard Bird","Yard Birds","Yardb